{"name":"Ode to Joy","hex":"#9d404a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ode","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A short poetical composition proper to be set to music or sung; a lyric poem; especially, now, a poem characterized by sustained noble sentiment and appropriate dignity of style."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An odonate; a dragonfly or damselfly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ode"},{"term":"joy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A feeling of extreme happiness or cheerfulness, especially related to the acquisition or expectation of something good.","Anything that causes such a feeling."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Expressing appreciation and happiness."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/joy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ode to Joy","blocks":[{"text":"\"Ode to Joy\" is an ode written in the summer of 1785 by the German poet, playwright, and historian Friedrich Schiller. It was published the following year in the German magazine Thalia. In 1808, a slightly revised version changed two lines of the first stanza and omitted the last stanza."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Schiller_an_die_freude_manuskript_2.jpg/330px-Schiller_an_die_freude_manuskript_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ode_to_Joy","wikidata":"Q41545"},{"title":"Ode to Joy (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Ode to Joy is a 2016 Chinese television series jointly produced by Shandong Television Media Group and Daylight Entertainment Television Ltd. It is based on the same title novel by A Nai. The first season of the drama aired from 18 April to 10 May 2016."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c0/Ode_to_Joy_Season_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ode_to_Joy_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q24836988"},{"title":"Ode","blocks":[{"text":"An ode is a type of lyric poetry, with its origins in Ancient Greece. Odes are elaborately structured poems praising or glorifying an event or individual, describing nature intellectually as well as emotionally. A classic ode is structured in three major parts: the strophe, the antistrophe, and the epode. Different forms such as the homostrophic ode and the irregular ode also enter."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ode","wikidata":"Q178985"},{"title":"Joy","blocks":[{"text":"Joy is the state of being that allows one to experience feelings of intense, long-lasting happiness and contentment of life. It is closely related to, and often evoked by, well-being, success, or good fortune. Happiness, pleasure, and gratitude are closely related to joy but are not identical to it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/A_Smiling_boy_from_Bangladesh.jpg/330px-A_Smiling_boy_from_Bangladesh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joy","wikidata":"Q935526"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Schillerhaus_Menckestrasse_Leipzig_2009.jpg/500px-Schillerhaus_Menckestrasse_Leipzig_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Schillerhaus_Menckestrasse_Leipzig_2009.jpg/1280px-Schillerhaus_Menckestrasse_Leipzig_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Schillerhaus_Menckestrasse_Leipzig_2009.jpg/500px-Schillerhaus_Menckestrasse_Leipzig_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Schillerhaus in Gohlis","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASchillerhaus_Menckestrasse_Leipzig_2009.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Books_an